0..35 Comment "//! The binding field in rule terms"
36..129 Comment "//! [Kaposi-2024-secondorder_generalised_algebraic_theories_signatures_firstorder_semantics]."
130..210 Comment "//! At a port written `pi+ (x : S) . T` a rule writes `bind x . t` for the field"
211..285 Comment "//! the port binds: `x` is a variable of the representable sort `S`, which"
286..362 Comment "//! substitution instantiates. At a port written `bind (a : N) . T` the same"
363..443 Comment "//! spelling abstracts the atom `a` (`bind-term.gandr`), which swapping renames."
444..521 Comment "//! The port decides which: the value of `Theory` keeps a field as `Bind` and"
522..601 Comment "//! its variable as `Bvar`, an abstraction as `Abs` and its atom as `Occ`, so a"
602..652 Comment "//! program tells the two binders apart by `case`."
653..656 Comment "//!"
657..758 Comment "//! - cites: [Kaposi-2024-secondorder_generalised_algebraic_theories_signatures_firstorder_semantics]"
759..762 Comment "//!"
763..962 Comment "//! [Kaposi-2024-secondorder_generalised_algebraic_theories_signatures_firstorder_semantics]: https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.FSCD.2024.10 \"Kaposi and Xie, Second-Order Generalised Algebraic Theories\""
964..1038 Comment "/// A receive on a restricted channel: `nu` abstracts the channel `c`, and"
1039..1115 Comment "/// `listen`\'s continuation is a field binding the value `x` received on it."
1116..1189 Comment "/// No process outside the restriction can name `c` to send on it, so the"
1190..1265 Comment "/// receive never fires. The checker orients the law and the kernel replays"
1266..1282 Comment "/// the verdict."
